"Where is AI?"




Students identify AI systems they interact with every day and classify:

What the AI does
ChatGPT is a generative AI that can do many things such as answer questions from the user, generate images, text, code, etc...

What data it uses
ChatGPT uses public data as well as user data. Public data ChatGPT uses includes things such as websites, articles, newspapers, books, and other web pages. User data that ChatGPT 
uses is all the data that the user shares such as images, prompts, and files. 

What business problem it solves
A business problem that ChatGPT solves is that it can generate images for social media marketing, or marketing in general, which reduces time and is more efficient for the business
rather than creating marketing images to put on social media completely from scratch.

Who benefits
ChatGPT can benefit everyone that uses it. Whether it is businesses, institutions, students, or just everyday users.

What could go wrong
ChatGPT is known to generate false data or references. This could be harmful if businesses use the false data as it could affect credibility. 
